VALUES
 ('GAP-304','EG','P1','OPEN','multilingual-research','energy-conservation-rest-points-seating',
  'Rest-point INTERVAL has no primary-evidence basis at any tier. UK DfT Inclusive Mobility s4.5 gives 50m (urban) and p124 gives 100m (countryside); ASLA gives 20m but its sole citation contains no spacing figure. Wheels for Wellbeing 50m cites Inclusive Mobility, so it is a restatement and not independent corroboration. No T1/T2/T3 study located that measures the distance at which people with sustained-exertion demand require rest. The NEED is evidenced at full band; the VALUE is weak band only.',
  'Falsified if a primary study is found that measures rest-requirement distance for any population with elevated sustained-exertion demand, or if a standards body publishes the derivation behind the 50m figure.',
  '2026-07-25','session_2026-07-25-energy-conservation-rest-points-seating','2026-07-25','session_2026-07-25-energy-conservation-rest-points-seating','ADDRESSABLE'),

 ('GAP-305','CD','P2','OPEN','cell-curator','jurisdictional_values',
  'jurisdictional_values.item_code is NOT NULL and FKs to items(item_code), so clause-cited code values discovered during SLUG-STAGE research have no structured home. This batch verified DfT Inclusive Mobility s4.5 p31 (50m), p102 (seat dims) and p124 (100m) to clause level but could not file them without fabricating an item_code. Values are currently held in the source notes and search log only, which is exactly the prose-not-structure failure R12 exists to prevent.',
  'Falsified if a slug-scoped value table exists or item_code is made nullable with a slug alternative.',
  '2026-07-25','session_2026-07-25-energy-conservation-rest-points-seating','2026-07-25','session_2026-07-25-energy-conservation-rest-points-seating','NOT-ADDRESSABLE'),

 ('GAP-306','RP','P2','OPEN','citation-miner','energy-conservation-rest-points-seating',
  'The two quantitative cohorts admitted for this slug (REF-00945, REF-00946) share authors and institution (Jyvaskyla; Rantakokko, Rantanen, Iwarsson) and REF-00948 shares that group again. Three of four primary admissions therefore trace to one research group and largely one Finnish cohort tradition. Independence of the resting-places finding is UNTESTED. Backward/forward mining must be constructed to escape the cluster rather than confirm it.',
  'Falsified if an independent group in a different country replicates the association between absence of resting places and reduced outdoor activity or quality of life.',
  '2026-07-25','session_2026-07-25-energy-conservation-rest-points-seating','2026-07-25','session_2026-07-25-energy-conservation-rest-points-seating','ADDRESSABLE');

